# ---- Round 9: terms from the acts themselves (Statutes at Large, Library of Congress scans) ----
("stat-1836-unmarried","LOC_C24","widow shall be entitled to receive, during the time she may remain unmarried","1836 act: the widow was paid only while she stayed unmarried.","5 Stat. 128, sec. 3"),
("stat-1838-1832-service","LOC_C25","who served in the war of the Revolution, in the manner specified in the act passed the seventh day of June, eighteen hundred and thirty-two","1838 act: the husband's service had to be the kind described in the act of June 7, 1832.","5 Stat. 303"),
("stat-1838-after-service","LOC_C25","whose marriage took place after the expiration of the last period of his service, and before the first day of January, seventeen hundred and ninety-four","1838 act: the marriage had to come after his last period of service ended and before January 1, 1794.","5 Stat. 303"),
("stat-1838-remarriage","LOC_C25","in the event of the marriage of such widow, said annuity or pension shall be discontinued","1838 act: the pension stopped if the widow married again.","5 Stat. 303"),
("stat-1848-service","LOC_C30","who shall have served in the Continental line, State troops, volunteers, militia, or in the naval service, in the revolutionary war with Great Britain","1848 act: the husband had served in the Continental line, State troops, volunteers, militia or the naval service.","9 Stat. 265"),
("stat-1848-widowhood","LOC_C30","their husbands during such widowhood, of equal amount per annum","1848 act: the pension was paid during her widowhood.","9 Stat. 266"),
("stat-1848-no-second","LOC_C30","no widow now receiving a pension shall be entitled to","1848 act: a widow already receiving a pension could not get a further one under it.","9 Stat. 266"),
("stat-1848-cutoff","LOC_C30","no widow married after the first day of January, one thousand eight hundred, shall be entitled to receive","1848 act: no widow married after January 1, 1800 was covered.","9 Stat. 266"),
("stat-1855-revwar","LOC_C33","the officers and soldiers of the revolutionary war, or their widows or minor children, shall be entitled to the","1855 bounty-land act: it extended to Revolutionary War officers and soldiers, their widows and minor children.","10 Stat. 702, sec. 8"),
("stat-1855-14-days","LOC_C33","in no case shall any such certificate or warrant be issued for any service less than fourteen days, except where the person shall actually have been engaged in battle","1855 bounty-land act: no warrant for under 14 days of service unless he was actually in a battle.","10 Stat. 702, sec. 3"),
("stat-1855-mustered","LOC_C33","called into military service, and regularly mustered therein, and whose services have been paid by the United States","1855 bounty-land act: militia, volunteers or State troops had to be regularly mustered, with service paid by the United States.","10 Stat. 701, sec. 1"),
("stat-1855-deserted","LOC_C33","if it shall appear by the muster-rolls of his regiment or corps that he deserted, or was dishonorably discharged from service","1855 bounty-land act: no warrant if the muster rolls show he deserted or was dishonorably discharged.","10 Stat. 702, sec. 1"),
("stat-1855-widow-at-application","LOC_C33","a subsequent marriage shall not impair the right of any such widow to such warrant if she be a widow at the time of making her application","1855 bounty-land act: remarriage didn't bar a widow if she was a widow when she applied.","10 Stat. 702, sec. 2"),
("stat-1878-14-days-a","LOC_C45","any widow of a Revolutionary soldier who served fourteen","1878 act: a widow of a Revolutionary soldier who served 14 days or was in any engagement was to be pensioned.","20 Stat. 29, sec. 6"),
("stat-1878-14-days-b","LOC_C45","days or was in any engagement shall be placed upon the pension-rolls","1878 act: the 14-day rule also accepted a soldier who was in any engagement.","20 Stat. 29, sec. 6"),
("stat-1878-remarriage","LOC_C45","the pensions to widows provided for in this act shall cease when they shall marry again","1878 act: widows' pensions ended if they married again.","20 Stat. 28, sec. 2"),
("stat-1878-eight-dollars","LOC_C45","this act shall not apply to any person who is receiving a pension at the rate of eight dollars per month or more","1878 act: it did not apply to anyone already receiving a pension of $8 a month or more.","20 Stat. 28, sec. 2"),
("stat-1853-army","LOC_C32","non-commissioned officers, musicians, and privates of the Revolutionary","1853 act: it covered widows of officers, non-commissioned officers, musicians and privates of the Revolutionary army.","10 Stat. 154, sec. 2"),
("stat-1853-after-1800","LOC_C32","who were married subsequent to January, anno Domini eighteen","1853 act: it covered those widows who were married after January 1800.","10 Stat. 154, sec. 2"),
("stat-1853-same-manner","LOC_C32","shall be entitled to a pension in the same manner as those who were married before that date","1853 act: they were pensioned in the same manner as widows married before that date.","10 Stat. 154, sec. 2"),
("stat-1855feb-navy","LOC_C33","non-commissioned officers, marines or mariners who served in the navy","February 1855 act: it covered widows of navy officers, non-commissioned officers, marines or mariners of the Revolutionary War.","10 Stat. 616, sec. 3"),
("stat-1855feb-1800","LOC_C33","since the first day of January, eighteen hundred, shall be entitled to","February 1855 act: it covered those widows married since January 1, 1800.","10 Stat. 616, sec. 3"),
("stat-1855feb-same","LOC_C33","section of the act of February third, eighteen hundred and fifty-three","February 1855 act: their pensions were in the same manner as army widows under section 2 of the 1853 act.","10 Stat. 616, sec. 3"),
("nara-natf85-order","NARA_ORDER","to order copies of military pension application files based on Federal (not State or Confederate) service between 1775 and","The National Archives' NATF Form 85 orders copies of federal military pension files for service from 1775.",None),
("nara-natf85-revwar","NARA_ORDER","A Federal pre-Civil War military pension application based on Federal military service before the Civil War (for example, the Revolutionary War and War of 1812)","A NATF Form 85 order can be for a pre-Civil War pension file, such as a Revolutionary War file.",None),
("m805-selected","M804","microfilm publication, Selected Records From Revolutionary War Pension and","The selected records from the pension files were also filmed as a separate publication, Selected Records From Revolutionary War Pension and Bounty-Land-Warrant Application Files.","PDF p. 5"),
